--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (3/3 key facts kept) ---
I spoke to Mr. Walter Thomas about the news in the morning paper, because I was anxious to learn if the German fleet had been defeated. Arthur made a mistake in his ledger, and I had to call him to account for it. I pawned my husband's watch, because I wanted some money. Bert gave me his half of the week's rent, and I was pleased and thankful.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks she is a nice child.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks Mr. Thomas a competent chief.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (3/4 key facts kept) ---
I found my half-crown, spoke to Thomas about the work, was paid wages, and made a mistake in the ledger; all very annoying, but not worrying.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: Mr. Thomas thinks Mr. Hale a careless young man, who may improve, but is not to be trusted at present.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: Mr. Thomas thinks well of Mrs. Turner.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (3/3 key facts kept) ---
I spoke to Arthur about a wrong entry in the ledger, and I rebuked him. Afterwards I found a half-crown under his desk, which pleased me. Finally I spoke to Mr. Hale about the work in hand, and I was satisfied.

