--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Saturday, the 15th of March, 1930 (1/2 key facts kept) ---
I spoke to Bert about the day at the docks, and he said it had been bad. The arrivals had been few, and the departures nil. So there was nothing for us to do. The weather had been foggy and cold, and the men had stood about disconsolately. Bert came home to dinner at one o'clock, and after dinner we went out and did some shopping. I bought a pound of tea and a quartern loaf, and he bought a pipe and some baccy. We had tea at five, and at half past six went to bed.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks Mr. Thomas careless.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks Mrs. Hale a good little woman.

