--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Thursday, the 27th of March, 1930 (1/1 key facts kept) ---
I spoke with Mrs. Edith Hale about how the day has gone. It has been fine, and I have been busy. In the morning I went to the City, and all day long I have been at work in the office. In the evening I came home, and read the paper. Joan and I talked together. The day has passed quietly, and I am glad to have done with it.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks him a steady young man.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Thursday, the 27th of March, 1930 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I spoke with Mr. Arthur Hale about the work in hand, and was glad to find that he had got on so well with it. I spoke with him also about the news in the paper, and thought it rather stormy.

